{
  "id": "murphy-shiva-erp-septum-chirp-chirp",
  "name": "Shiva modulated 40 Hz chirp (alone)",
  "category": "signals",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "origin": "Shiva software by Todd Murphy (signal templates licensed from Persinger and Koren)",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's simple Shiva chirp session: the 'modulated 40 Hz chirp' stepped counter-clockwise around the head, which Murphy presents for altered states. He advises using it within sessions with several phases, and not by itself until you have used Shiva in other ways.",
  "setting": "Dark, quiet room, eyes closed, relaxed without meditating or falling asleep.",
  "schedule": "At most once a week, never on consecutive days; up to 6 sessions, then a 21-day break.",
  "notes": "Coils sit on Murphy's Shiva ring (Fp1, FT7, TP7, O1, O2, TP8, FT8, Fp2; one coil per site instead of Shiva's coil pairs) and fire one at a time counter-clockwise seen from above (back-to-front over the right side), 10, 12 … 20 ms per coil (Murphy's lecture example; Shiva's own step table is unpublished). The 'modulated 40 Hz chirp' file is proprietary. Murphy says the Shiva chirp 'does not change in tone, but rather has longer and longer gaps between sections of the signal', and his Shakti chirp page says it starts from the modulated 40 Hz signal, with the frequency modulation applied to the gaps and a Fibonacci constant varying both the amplitude and the gap lengths. This file is a project construct after that description, not the Shiva file: twelve 125-ms sections of the project's modulated 40 Hz stand-in (40 Hz carrier, 0.5 Hz phase modulation, depth 3; 1-ms points), alternating between full and 0.618 amplitude, separated by gaps that grow along the Fibonacci series (3, 5, 8 … 377 ms), then 1.5 s of silence, so the pattern repeats every 4 s like the lab's frequency-modulated pattern, to which Murphy relates the chirp (Dixon & Persinger 2001; Tiller & Persinger 2002). The real section lengths, gap series and amplitudes are unpublished. Shiva's simple sessions usually come in 20, 30 and 60-min versions; this file runs 20. Murphy warns that the chirp 'can be very unpleasant over the right side' (Shakti chirp page). Independent double-blind tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005; Gendle & McGrath 2012). Stop at once on fear or distress; not for people with epilepsy.",
  "source": "Murphy, Shiva demo: Chirp signal https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/shiva/shiva_demo/mod40_chirp.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Modulated 40 Hz chirp signal https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/mod40_chirp_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shiva demo: Sessions used in lab experiments (Shiva chirp description) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/shiva/shiva_demo/experiment_signals.htm ; Dixon & Persinger 2001, Int J Neurosci 108:87 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11328704/ ; Tiller & Persinger 2002, Percept Mot Skills 94:26 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11883572/ ; Murphy, Shiva demo: Magnetic coil locations https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/shiva/shiva_demo/locations.htm ; Murphy, Psychic Skills & Miracles lecture (coil steps of 10, 12 ... 20 ms) https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tmC1174POpA ; Murphy, Shiva demo: Session lengths https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/shiva/shiva_demo/session_length.htm ; Granqvist et al. 2005, Neurosci Lett 379:1 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15849873/ ; Gendle & McGrath 2012, Percept Mot Skills 114:217 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22582690/",
